  242: #    *  it proves FORWARDING HAPPENED at all (a refusal prints nothing);
  243: #    *  it names WHERE the decode landed -- so this is an ANCHORED row in the carrier's clause-(f)
  244: #       sense, absolute rather than relative.  "If every address in this device shifted, which row
  245: #       reds?"  THIS one: the printed tuple changes.  A distinctness or survival oracle cannot see
  246: #       a translation at all;
  247: #    *  its ABSENCE at the bus-zero address proves the type-1/bus-0 alias is REFUSED rather than
  248: #       forwarded onto the primary bus -- which is the misrouting the repair exists to prevent, and
  249: #       which no survival oracle can observe because a misroute survives happily.
  250: #
  251: #  ADDRESS DERIVATION, from the handler's own two lines rather than from a table:
  252: #
  253: #      reg = (relative_addr >> 5) & 0xfc          tag = (relative_addr >> 5) & ~0xff
  254: #      type-1:  bus = (tag >> 16) & 0xff   dev = (tag >> 11) & 0x1f   func = (tag >> 8) & 7
  255: #      type-0:  dev = first d with tag & (0x800U << d)
  256: #
  257: #      bus 1, dev 3, func 2, reg 0  ->  tag = 0x11a00  ->  relative_addr = 0x234000
