  327: # ---- SESSION 2b: the REFUSAL'S RETURN VALUE ------------------------------------------------------
  328: #  *** THIS ROW EXISTS BECAUSE I ENUMERATED THE CLAUSE-(d) CLOSURE AND FOUND MY OWN ANSWER WRONG. ***
  329: #  Writing the pass-2 brief I claimed the (type-1, bus == 0, READ) cell was unobservable, "because it
  330: #  returns the same all-ones value as the control".  That reasoning conflates two different accesses:
  331: #  the control is a TYPE-0 empty-slot read, and this is the REFUSAL arm's own synthesised value.  They
  332: #  agree on the fix and they do NOT agree under a mutant.
  333: #
  334: #  The refusal's repair is one expression -- `odata = reg == 0? (uint64_t) -1 : 0'.  NULL IT
